menu "bitEngine Configuration"

    choice BITENGINE_PROFILE
        prompt "Product profile"
        default BITENGINE_PROFILE_HA
        help
            两种产品配置的总开关（docs/15_muse_direct_architecture_v1.md 5.8 R-1，设计 2.1 / 2.7）。
            编译期决定，没有运行时切换；换配置 = 给 C5 换固件。

            - HA：现有产品。桥接（ZHA / Z2M 经 :6638），Wi-Fi + 以太网，不带 Muse。
            - Direct：直连型（网关自己当 Zigbee 主机 + Matter 控制器 + Muse）。纯以太网、另一张分区表、没有桥。
              开发中，不发版。

            ⚠️ 不要在 menuconfig 里切它。直连型有自己的 sdkconfig 和构建目录：
                idf.py -B build-direct -DSDKCONFIG=sdkconfig.direct \
                       -DSDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.defaults.direct" \
                       -DBITENGINE_PROFILE=direct build
            （或 bash tools/build_profiles.sh）。顶层 CMakeLists.txt 核对这里的选择与 -DBITENGINE_PROFILE
            一致，不一致就停：防止拿 HA 型的 sdkconfig 编出一个叫 bitengine-direct 的固件，或者反过来。

            直连型专属的选项一律 depends on BITENGINE_PROFILE_DIRECT（tools/check_profile_rules.py 钉着）。

        config BITENGINE_PROFILE_HA
            bool "HA (bridge, Wi-Fi + Ethernet) — the shipping product"
        config BITENGINE_PROFILE_DIRECT
            bool "Direct (Hub + Muse, Ethernet only) — in development"
    endchoice

    config BITENGINE_NET_ETH_ONLY
        bool "Ethernet-only network profile (no Wi-Fi)"
        depends on BITENGINE_PROFILE_DIRECT
        default y
        help
            纯以太网剖面（docs/15 设计 2.2）：不初始化、也不链接 Wi-Fi。network_mgr 编 wifi_none.c 代替
            wifi_mgr.c / wifi_probe.c（"没有 Wi-Fi"的空实现：没有凭据、连不上、热点起不来、netif 为 NULL），
            其余直接调 esp_wifi_* 的地方都在 #if !CONFIG_BITENGINE_NET_ETH_ONLY 里；网页不注册 /wifi/*、
            /network/softap，/api/v1/status 带 "wifi":"absent"。省出的内部内存见架构 4.3（G0-3：+58 KB）。

            只在直连型里可见（架构 5.8 R-1）；HA 型永远带 Wi-Fi。

    config BITENGINE_ENABLE_ZHUB
        bool
        depends on BITENGINE_PROFILE_DIRECT
        default y
        help
            网关自己当 Zigbee 主机（Hub 模式，docs/15 设计 2.1 / 第八节）。**它同时决定桥编不编**（架构 5.8 R-2）：
            为 y 时不编 :6638 的 TCP 服务（tcp_server.c）与经 USB 的桥（usb_bridge.c）、SMLIGHT 兼容层（/api2/*），
            不宣告 _zigbee-bridge / _zigbee-coordinator，不注册只服务 :6638 的端点（/mode、/whitelist、
            /zigbee/clients/disconnect）；MG24 的 UART 照常建（ezsp_bridge_init_uart_only），留给 NCP 升级与将来的 zhub。
            直连型里也绝不走 IO23 复位 MG24。
            zhub 本身在 M4 进来；在那之前直连型没有 Zigbee 功能（Zigbee 灯灭 = 未启用），这是开发中间态，不发版。
            不可见、跟着总开关走：没有"直连型带桥"这种组合，也没有运行时开关（R-2）。

    config BITENGINE_ENABLE_MUSE_LINK
        bool "Muse direct link (pairing + session)"
        depends on BITENGINE_PROFILE_DIRECT && SPIRAM
        select BT_ENABLED
        default n
        help
            直连 Muse（docs/15 设计第四、五节）：编进 ble_window、muse_pair（社区配对 v5）、muse_link（VM API 与会话）
            与 noise_core（Noise XX 协议核心）。
            协议代码原样取自上游 muse-gadget-sdk，提交与逐文件哈希见 components/muse_link/UPSTREAM.md。
            BLE 只经 components/ble_window 用（配对窗口），策略见 BITENGINE_BLE_WINDOW_POLICY。
            sdkconfig.defaults.direct 把它打开；只在直连型里可见（架构 5.8 R-1）。

    config BITENGINE_ENABLE_MATTER_CTRL
        bool "Matter controller (client-only, on-network commissioning)"
        depends on BITENGINE_NET_ETH_ONLY && BITENGINE_ENABLE_MUSE_LINK
        default n
        help
            直连型的 Matter 控制器（docs/15 设计第九节）：esp-matter 的 client-only 控制器 + commissioner，用网关自己的 fabric，
            不带 server、不带 BLE、不接管 OpenThread（9.2）。只在纯以太网剖面开放（架构 4.3：省出的内部内存才放得下 CHIP）。
            sdkconfig.defaults.direct 把它打开，CHIP 的那一组选项也在那里（9.2 的表 + 9.8a）。
            esp_matter 由 components/matter_ctrl/idf_component.yml 带进来，只在直连型里解算、锁在 dependencies.direct.lock；
            HA 型的产物里没有它（tools/check_profiles.py）。

    config BITENGINE_MATTER_MAX_NODES
        int "Max Matter nodes on the hub's fabric"
        depends on BITENGINE_ENABLE_MATTER_CTRL
        range 1 128
        default 128
        help
            网关 fabric 上最多管多少个 Matter 节点（设计 2.1；节点表 hubdb/mctrl，9.3）。
            2026-10-24 用户定 32 → 128：节点表、访谈 / 订阅表都在 PSRAM，CHIP 的会话池 / 定时器池 / 交换上下文跟着放大（也在 PSRAM，
            components/matter_ctrl/CHIPProjectConfig.h 与 sdkconfig.defaults.direct）。结构上限 MC_NODES_CAP（mc_nodes_core.h）。
            ⚠️ 不是"网关能代播几台"：那是 CONFIG_MDNS_MAX_SERVICES 管的（tools/check_capacity_docs.py），配进本 fabric 的设备每台多占一条代播。

    choice BITENGINE_BLE_WINDOW_POLICY
        prompt "BLE window policy (how BLE and Thread share the radio)"
        depends on BITENGINE_ENABLE_MUSE_LINK
        default BITENGINE_BLE_WINDOW_POLICY_ISOLATED
        help
            BLE 窗口与 Thread 怎么分时用射频（docs/15 设计 3.2、2.1）。

            眼下只有 C（隔离重启）：配对时网关重启进一个不起 Thread 的配对剖面，配完再重启回正常模式。
            A（并存）/ B（暂停 Thread）要等 G0-4 的共存实测（#1851：BLE 反初始化后 Thread 收不到 ACK），
            通过了再加进这里；没实测之前不提供，免得选了一个没验证过的策略。

        config BITENGINE_BLE_WINDOW_POLICY_ISOLATED
            bool "C: isolated restart (pairing in a Thread-free boot profile)"
    endchoice

    config BITENGINE_MUSE_PAIR_WINDOW_S
        int "Muse pairing window (seconds)"
        depends on BITENGINE_ENABLE_MUSE_LINK
        range 60 600
        default 180
        help
            配对窗口的上限（设计 2.1、5.1）：从配对剖面里开始广播算起，到时没配完就关窗口、重启回正常模式。

    config BITENGINE_MUSE_API_URL
        string "Muse API base URL (default)"
        depends on BITENGINE_ENABLE_MUSE_LINK
        default "https://api.muse.ai"
        help
            VM API 的默认地址（设计 2.1、4.5）。配对时服务端下发的 api_url_v2（验过 https://）优先。

    config BITENGINE_MUSE_NOISE_HOST
        string "Muse Noise host (default)"
        depends on BITENGINE_ENABLE_MUSE_LINK
        default "hatch.metaaivm.com"
        help
            会话（TLS + WebSocket + Noise）连的主机（设计 2.1、4.6）。配对时下发的 noise_host 优先。

    config BITENGINE_MUSE_DEVICE_FAMILY
        string
        depends on BITENGINE_ENABLE_MUSE_LINK
        default "homehub"
        help
            link.register 的 device_family（设计 4.7、架构 MD-4；2026-10-22 G0-2 定为 homehub）。
            不给提示符：是编译期常量，定下后改默认值，不做运行时开关。

    config BITENGINE_MUSE_MODEL_ID
        string
        depends on BITENGINE_ENABLE_MUSE_LINK
        default "bitengine-hub-c5"
        help
            link.register 的 model_id（同上；备选是官方 ESP32 固件的 esp-link）。

    config BITENGINE_MUSE_MIN_INTERNAL_FREE
        int "Muse session memory gate: minimum free internal RAM (bytes)"
        depends on BITENGINE_ENABLE_MUSE_LINK
        range 4096 65536
        default 8192
        help
            会话的内存闸门（设计 4.6、N2）：进 FETCH_VM 前内部空闲不到这个数就进 LOW_MEM，60 s 复查。

    config BITENGINE_MUSE_MIN_DMA_FREE
        int "Muse session memory gate: minimum free DMA-capable RAM (bytes)"
        depends on BITENGINE_ENABLE_MUSE_LINK
        range 2048 32768
        default 4096
        help
            同上，DMA 可用内存（TLS 的 AES 走 DMA）。

    config BITENGINE_DIAG_MUSE_FAULT
        bool "Diagnostic build: inject a fetch_vms 401 into the Muse session (TC-MU09)"
        depends on BITENGINE_ENABLE_MUSE_LINK
        default n
        help
            故障注入构建（docs/15 设计 14.4 TC-MU09；N7 故障隔离的用例）。开机后取 VM 不发请求、直接当 401，
            走状态机的刷新路径，按下面的方式。⚠️ 方式 1 会清掉配对凭据（这正是要验的"撤销"），要重新配对。
            诊断构建：tools/publish_ota.sh 拒发任何开着 CONFIG_BITENGINE_DIAG_* 的构建。

    config BITENGINE_MUSE_FAULT_MODE
        int "TC-MU09 mode: 1 = refresh also rejected (token_revoked), 2 = refresh succeeds"
        depends on BITENGINE_DIAG_MUSE_FAULT
        range 1 2
        default 2
        help
            1：第一次取 VM 当 401，刷新也当被拒（不发请求）→ token_revoked、清令牌、进 UNPAIRED；
            2：头两次取 VM 当 401，中间的刷新真的去发（成功）→ credentials_refused，按 1–30 min 退避、保留配对，之后正常上线。
            计数每次开机从 0 起：方式 1 验完之后在同一份诊断固件上重新配对，配对剖面回来那次开机会又被"撤销"一次 ——
            验完先刷回正常固件再配对。

    config BITENGINE_DIAG_HUBDB
        bool "Diagnostic endpoint /api/v1/diag/hubdb (development)"
        depends on BITENGINE_PROFILE_DIRECT
        default n
        help
            开发期的诊断端点（docs/15 设计 2.5）：GET 读 hub_store 的状态和一个探针键（hub/diag_probe），
            POST {"text":"…"} 写它、{"erase":true} 删它、{"flush":true} 立即落盘。用来上板验 hubdb 读写、
            防抖、重启后读回。sdkconfig.defaults.direct 在开发期把它打开；直连型发版前必须关掉。

    config BITENGINE_WIFI_KCONFIG_FALLBACK
        bool "Use Kconfig WiFi credentials when NVS is empty (DEV ONLY)"
        default n
        help
            Development convenience: auto-connect using the SSID/password
            below when no credentials are stored in NVS. MUST be disabled
            for production — factory-fresh devices need to enter SoftAP
            provisioning immediately.

    config BITENGINE_WIFI_SSID
        string "WiFi SSID"
        depends on BITENGINE_WIFI_KCONFIG_FALLBACK
        default "MyNetwork"
        help
            WiFi network name (5GHz only).

    config BITENGINE_WIFI_PASSWORD
        string "WiFi Password"
        depends on BITENGINE_WIFI_KCONFIG_FALLBACK
        default "password"
        help
            WiFi network password.

    config BITENGINE_TCP_PORT
        int "EZSP TCP port"
        default 6638
        help
            TCP port for EZSP bridge (Zigbee2MQTT / ZHA connects here).

    config BITENGINE_HAS_ETHERNET
        bool "Enable Ethernet (DM9051)"
        default n
        help
            Enable Ethernet support. Requires DM9051 SPI PHY hardware.
            Enabled on PCB via sdkconfig.defaults.

    config BITENGINE_PSRAM_SELFTEST
        bool "Run PSRAM self-test after watchdog feed starts"
        default y
        depends on SPIRAM
        help
            App-level replacement for CONFIG_SPIRAM_MEMTEST (disabled because
            it runs before the first RS706 WDI feed and trips the 1.6s HW
            watchdog). Tests all free PSRAM heap regions synchronously in
            app_main, after watchdog_init() and before network_mgr_init().
            Adds roughly 1s to boot. Failure is logged but does not halt boot.

    config BITENGINE_HAS_HW_WATCHDOG
        bool "Enable RS706 Hardware Watchdog"
        default n
        help
            Enable RS706 hardware watchdog WDI toggling via GPIO.
            Disabled for DevKit stage (no RS706 chip).

    config BITENGINE_WS2812_T0H_NS
        int "WS2812 T0H pulse width (ns)"
        default 150
        range 60 400
        help
            0-bit high time. Standard WS2812 is 300ns; this PCB's transistor
            level shifter widens every pulse by ~150-250ns (X5), so 150ns
            pre-compensates to ~300-400ns on the wire — centred in the
            WS2812B T0H spec (220-380ns). Whether it goes back to 300 depends
            on what AM2 fits in place of the shifter (AM2 work order A2).

    config BITENGINE_WS2812_T1H_NS
        int "WS2812 T1H pulse width (ns)"
        default 550
        range 300 1000
        help
            1-bit high time. Standard is 900ns. Measured on the production
            PCB 2026-08-13 (four-white criterion, /api/v1/led/timing):

              T1H  250 300 | 400 550 600 700 | 850
                    灭  灭 |  好  好  好  好 | 丢字节

            Below ~400 the widened pulse still misses the 0/1 decision
            threshold, every bit reads as 0 and the whole chain goes dark.
            Above ~700 the low gap (1200-T1H-widening) gets eaten, runs of
            1-bits merge and every byte AFTER the first non-zero one is lost.
            550 is the centre of that window (~150ns margin each side).

            ⚠️ Verify with WHITE, never a single-channel colour. Red is
            `00 FF 00` on the wire — nothing follows its first non-zero byte,
            so the byte-loss failure is invisible to it. T1H=850 shipped for
            months because the sweep used red as its criterion.

            Set back to 900 after the X5 hardware fix.

    config BITENGINE_HAS_WS2812B
        bool "Enable WS2812B LED"
        default n
        help
            Enable WS2812B RGB LED via RMT driver.
            Disabled for DevKit stage (not wired).

    config BITENGINE_HAS_BUTTON
        bool "Enable hardware button"
        default n
        help
            Enable physical button on GPIO.
            Disabled for DevKit stage (not wired).

    config BITENGINE_HAS_MG24_RESET_PIN
        bool "Enable MG24 Hardware Reset Pin"
        default n
        help
            Enable MG24 nRESET control via GPIO for hard reset.
            Disabled for DevKit stage (pin not wired).

    config BITENGINE_MG24_RESET_ISOLATED
        bool "MG24 reset line is isolated from the supervisor (AM2 and later)"
        depends on BITENGINE_HAS_MG24_RESET_PIN
        default n
        help
            Set this on boards where R113 is a diode (anode = ZIGBEE_RESET,
            cathode = RS706 RESET) plus the added 10K pull-up on the
            ZIGBEE_RESET net — item A1 of docs/hardware/PCB_硬件待确认清单.md.

            On AM1 boards (default, n) driving IO23 low back-feeds the RS706's
            weak push-pull output through R67+R113; its RESET pin collapses,
            drags C5's EN down through R58, and the WHOLE BOARD resets. The
            firmware still offers the reset as a last resort for a wedged
            MG24, but says so — /api/v1/zigbee/status reports
            restart_resets_board so the WebUI can warn accordingly.

            Turning this on without the hardware change makes the UI promise a
            Zigbee-only restart while the gateway actually reboots. Only set it
            after verifying the diode and pull-up are populated.

    config BITENGINE_WIFI_DISABLE_PMF
        bool "Disable Wi-Fi Protected Management Frames (escape hatch)"
        default n
        help
            Leave OFF. PMF is negotiated whenever the AP supports it (IDF default,
            "PMF optional"); WPA3-only and PMF-required WPA2 routers need it.
            2026-03-30..2026-09-13 the firmware disabled PMF unconditionally, citing
            SA Query timeouts while the 802.15.4 (Thread) radio is active. That was
            never isolated; on the production PCB with IDF v6.0.2, 20 minutes of
            WPA3-SAE + pmf:1 under 53 back-to-back 802.15.4 active scans produced
            zero disconnects (docs/产品化TODO T2.17).
            Turn this on only if the field shows repeated STA disconnects with
            reason=209 (WIFI_REASON_SA_QUERY_TIMEOUT). Cost: WPA3-only APs cannot
            be joined at all.

    config BITENGINE_WIFI_FLOAT_ETH_IP
        bool "Float the Ethernet IP onto Wi-Fi during failover"
        default y
        help
            When Ethernet drops on a dual-uplink gateway, move the Ethernet's own IP
            (the address ZHA/OTBR/HA are configured to reach, e.g. socket://<eth-ip>:6638)
            onto the Wi-Fi interface as a static address and broadcast a gratuitous ARP.
            External fixed-IP clients then follow the active link automatically after one
            reconnect, with no Home Assistant reconfiguration. Requires both interfaces on
            the same L2 subnet (they are: the router bridges wired + 5GHz); since 2026-10-06
            this is checked: if the Ethernet IP is not inside Wi-Fi's own subnet the gateway
            logs a warning and keeps Wi-Fi on its own address. It also only floats while the
            configured Wi-Fi SSID is the one configured when Ethernet got the address (changing
            Wi-Fi networks with the cable out stops the float; switching back resumes it).
            The DNS servers Wi-Fi had are
            carried over (setting a static address clears lwIP's global DNS; before
            2026-10-06 name resolution failed for the whole float). The address is
            reclaimed onto Ethernet the instant its link returns.
            2026-09-14: without this, failover to Wi-Fi keeps only gateway-originated
            traffic alive; the Zigbee bridge (inbound, IP-bound) drops because ZHA cannot
            follow the address change (docs/产品化TODO T2.23).
            This state lives in RAM: a reboot while the cable is still out loses it — see
            BITENGINE_WIFI_FLOAT_BOOT_TAKEOVER below.
            No router reservation is required for short outages; a DHCP reservation only
            matters if an outage outlasts the lease (the float does not track the lease).
            Since T9.37 (BITENGINE_SVC_IDENTITY, default y) this static float is only the
            fallback: the service address normally moves between the interfaces by DHCP
            (see that option). The float here runs when the identity mechanism is not in
            charge: either interface has a static IP, or the service identity is Ethernet and
            the router keys leases by MAC only / the identity mechanism gave up for this boot
            (a Wi-Fi identity is pinned to Wi-Fi instead, see that option).

    config BITENGINE_WIFI_FLOAT_BOOT_TAKEOVER
        bool "Also take the Ethernet IP over at boot when the cable is still out"
        depends on BITENGINE_WIFI_FLOAT_ETH_IP
        default y
        help
            T9.20 (2026-10-06). Without this, rebooting while the Ethernet cable is out
            (power cut, watchdog, user reboot, reboot after an update) leaves Wi-Fi on its
            own DHCP address, and ZHA/OTBR (configured with the Ethernet IP) stay
            disconnected until the cable returns.
            While Ethernet holds a DHCP lease, the gateway stores the address, mask,
            gateway, lease expiry (wall clock) and a fingerprint of the configured Wi-Fi
            SSID in NVS (namespace "net_svc"; rewritten only when something changes or the
            lease is renewed, at most every lease/4 clamped to 5-30 min; not stored while
            no Wi-Fi is configured; erased by factory reset).
            At boot, once the cable is still absent 20 s after the network manager starts
            and Wi-Fi has its own address, the stored Ethernet IP is floated onto Wi-Fi only
            when ALL of these hold:
              - it is inside Wi-Fi's current subnet, and Wi-Fi is still the same SSID;
              - the lease has not expired (5 min margin), judged against a trusted wall
                clock: SNTP synced in this boot, or inherited from a previous boot that had
                a trusted clock across an esp_restart() (the RTC keeps time across it).
                After a power cut, or a crash / watchdog reset (main.c's extra restart after
                such a reset clears the inherited mark), it waits for SNTP; without Internet
                time it never takes over. An infinite lease (DHCP option 51 = 0xFFFFFFFF)
                skips the clock check;
              - an ARP request for the address (3 s window, sent from Wi-Fi's own address)
                gets no answer from another device. Blind spots: a device that is itself
                probing at that moment, or one that ignores ARP.
            Otherwise Wi-Fi keeps its own address and the gateway logs a W line starting
            with "开机接管：" (waiting for the clock, or why it refused); plugging the cable
            back in restores everything. Static Ethernet IPs have no lease to verify and
            are never taken over at boot (the runtime float still works for them).
            Once taken over, the address is held like a runtime float: until the cable
            returns; the lease is not tracked afterwards. The address is only floated while
            the configured Wi-Fi SSID is the one it was captured under (runtime float too):
            switching to another network drops it, switching back resumes it.
            Only a boot that actually took the address over counts as "fell back": when
            the cable returns, the address goes back to Ethernet and a RECOVERED event is
            posted (MQTT and the Thread border router follow Ethernet), same as a runtime
            failover. A boot that merely lacked Ethernet posts nothing (T2.16).
            /api/v1/status reports the outcome in svc_takeover; values and meaning:
            network_mgr_svc_takeover_state() in network_mgr.h.
            Rules: components/network_mgr/svc_policy.c (host test: test_host/run.sh).
            Turn off to stop storing the snapshot and taking it over at boot; the runtime
            float (including its subnet check and DNS carry-over) is unaffected.
            Since T9.37 (BITENGINE_SVC_IDENTITY) the snapshot is still stored, but the boot
            takeover only runs when the identity mechanism is not in charge (same cases as
            the runtime float above). The snapshot is also what an upgraded unit migrates
            from: same Wi-Fi network -> service identity = Ethernet, service address = the
            snapshot's address.

    config BITENGINE_MDNS_SVC_IP_ONLY
        bool "mDNS announces only the Ethernet service IP for this gateway's own name"
        depends on BITENGINE_WIFI_FLOAT_ETH_IP
        default y
        help
            T9.34 (2026-10-07). Without this, the stock mdns component (1.11.0) treats the
            Wi-Fi and Ethernet interfaces on the same subnet as duplicates, lets the one with
            the numerically larger address answer, and lists both addresses with its own
            first (captured on the bench: answers from the Wi-Fi address, A records
            [Wi-Fi, Ethernet]). HA / ZHA / Zigbee2MQTT record the first address when the
            gateway is added, so they can end up on the Wi-Fi address - and lose the gateway
            when the cable is pulled, because the Ethernet IP then floats onto Wi-Fi and
            replaces Wi-Fi's own address.
            With this on, the A record for <hostname>.local carries exactly one address.
            With BITENGINE_SVC_IDENTITY in charge (the default) that is the service address,
            announced as soon as it is known and kept even while no interface holds it
            (handover gap, boot grace): HA should record it, wherever it lives right now.
            Before it is known (first install), nothing for up to 60 s, then Wi-Fi's own
            address. The rest of this list is the fallback (identity not in charge):
              - the Ethernet service IP whenever Ethernet holds it (link up and addressed),
                it is floated onto Wi-Fi, or the cable was just plugged back in and
                Ethernet is still in DHCP (up to 10 s). On the Wi-Fi interface only if the
                service IP is inside Wi-Fi's subnet (or floated onto it): with Ethernet and
                Wi-Fi on different subnets, Wi-Fi keeps announcing its own address;
              - nothing (no A and no AAAA for the gateway's own name; services are still
                announced) while the service IP is not settled at boot: during the first
                60 s after the network manager starts, while the Ethernet link is up without
                an address or the boot takeover (BITENGINE_WIFI_FLOAT_BOOT_TAKEOVER) is still
                deciding; after 60 s Wi-Fi's own address is announced until that resolves.
                Also nothing on the Wi-Fi interface for the few seconds its address is 0
                (the service IP was just handed back and Wi-Fi is re-running DHCP);
              - Wi-Fi's own address otherwise (no Ethernet this boot, takeover refused,
                Ethernet DHCP failed, or the IP could not float: other SSID / subnet).
            When the address changes the gateway re-announces (and once more 2 s later, in
            case mdns dropped the first request); an announcement that carries only the
            gateway's own addresses puts them in the Answer section (stock: Authority) with
            the cache-flush bit, so caches that honour it (HA's zeroconf) drop the old
            address within 1 s (RFC 6762 10.2).
            On the same subnet one fixed interface answers and the other stays quiet: the
            stock duplicate detection relies on the two interfaces announcing different
            addresses, which no longer holds. Which one is decided in a single place,
            bitengine_if_answers() in tools/patch_mdns.py: Ethernet. Normally all mDNS,
            including the Thread/Matter proxy records, goes out the wire and stays off the
            radio Wi-Fi time-shares with Thread, and a Wi-Fi drop no longer moves the
            answering interface back and forth; Wi-Fi answers only while the cable is out
            (with the service IP floated onto it). On networks where Wi-Fi had the larger
            address (the bench), the proxy records move from Wi-Fi to Ethernet.
            mdns side: tools/patch_mdns.py group 4 (SVCIP), applied at build time.
            Rules: svc_mdns_decide() in components/network_mgr/svc_policy.c (host test:
            components/network_mgr/test_host/run.sh).
            A device that was installed over Wi-Fi only and later got a cable: with
            BITENGINE_SVC_IDENTITY its service address is Wi-Fi's original address and moves
            onto the cable, so both the announcement and a hand-typed address keep working.
            In the fallback the announcement moves to the Ethernet IP and a hand-typed Wi-Fi
            address does not.
            Turning this off restores the stock A record contents only; the mdns patches
            stay, so the same fixed interface (Ethernet) still answers - the Ethernet address
            then always comes first, deterministically, instead of whichever is larger.

    config BITENGINE_SVC_IDENTITY
        bool "Service address follows a DHCP identity (dual-direction float)"
        depends on BITENGINE_WIFI_FLOAT_ETH_IP && BITENGINE_WIFI_FLOAT_BOOT_TAKEOVER
        default y
        help
            T9.37 (2026-10-07). Design: docs/16_service_identity_dual_float_design_v1.md.
            The service address (the one HA / ZHA / Zigbee2MQTT / OTBR record, and the only
            one mDNS announces for this gateway) is the lease of a DHCP identity S
            (client-id, option 61), not "the Ethernet address". S is the client-id of the
            interface that first got an address on this network: Ethernet if the cable was
            in at install time, otherwise Wi-Fi. It is stored in NVS (namespace net_id) together
            with a fingerprint of the configured Wi-Fi SSID, and never re-decided by boot races.
            A factory reset deliberately keeps it (decided 2026-10-07): the address is not a
            user setting, and wiping it would re-decide a Wi-Fi-installed, later-cabled unit as
            "Ethernet", breaking the address HA recorded. While Wi-Fi is unconfigured after the
            reset a temporary first-install identity is used (RAM only); as soon as Wi-Fi gets an
            address on the recorded network again, the stored identity is resumed. It is re-decided (as a first install)
            when Wi-Fi gets an address on a different network, or the service address's
            subnet is on neither interface any more. While no Wi-Fi is configured (factory
            line) the identity stays in RAM only, so shipped units do not carry an
            "Ethernet" identity from the line test. Units upgraded from older firmware
            migrate from the boot-takeover snapshot (BITENGINE_WIFI_FLOAT_BOOT_TAKEOVER):
            same Wi-Fi network -> Ethernet, with the snapshot's address.
            The holder requests the lease with client-id S; the other interface uses the
            other interface's client-id (the two swap when the holder is not S's own NIC).
            Routers that key leases by client-id (RFC 2131; measured on the bench router)
            then give the service address to whichever interface holds it, and it renews
            normally there. Holder: Ethernet while its link is up and it has an address in
            the service subnet; otherwise Wi-Fi. At runtime a newly plugged cable first gets
            an address with the other identity (proving the wired path and that it is the
            same subnet); only then is the service address handed over. At boot with the
            cable in, Ethernet is presumed the holder (handed to Wi-Fi if its DHCP times out
            in 10 s; after two such timeouts on one link, Ethernet is not given it back until
            the link drops); with the cable out, the holder is decided after a 10 s link
            grace. Wi-Fi never holds the service address while it is on a different subnet
            and Ethernet is on the service subnet (two separate networks).
            Handover: both interfaces first switch to a dummy client-id and stop DHCP
            (esp_netif_dhcpc_stop sends a DHCPRELEASE; with the dummy id it matches no
            lease), then restart with their new ids. The old holder has dropped the address
            before the new one asks, so the DHCP ARP check sees no conflict. Gap: one DHCP
            round (2026-10-07 bench: ZHA reconnected 1.2 s after a cable plug-in handover and
            7.6 s after a cable pull); TCP connections on the old interface are reset and
            clients reconnect. The new holder sends gratuitous ARP 3 times.
            Example: installed on Wi-Fi (address .36), cable plugged later: Ethernet first
            gets .34 with its own id, then takes .36 (Wi-Fi switches to .34); HA keeps
            using .36 over the cable. Cable pulled: .36 moves back to Wi-Fi.
            Degraded mode. If S is Wi-Fi, the service address is pinned to Wi-Fi: both
            interfaces use their own client-id, Wi-Fi keeps the service address, Ethernet is
            just a second address (traffic to the service address uses Wi-Fi even with the
            cable in, but the address HA recorded never breaks); /api/v1/status reports
            svc_holder=wifi_pinned. If S is Ethernet, the old behaviour is used (service
            address = Ethernet address, static float onto Wi-Fi per
            BITENGINE_WIFI_FLOAT_ETH_IP, boot takeover), which keeps that address working.
            Degraded mode is entered:
              - recorded per Wi-Fi network: a swapped interface asking with S gets exactly
                the address it got earlier this boot with its own client-id - the router
                keys leases by MAC only. Retried at the first boot at least 7 days after
                it was recorded (counted on a trusted wall clock: SNTP, or inherited across
                esp_restart; stamped once the clock becomes trusted), so removing a DHCP
                reservation or replacing the router recovers by itself; changing Wi-Fi
                networks also retries;
              - this boot only (retried next boot): the swapped Wi-Fi gets no address for
                20 s after associating (some servers NAK or ignore a client-id from another
                MAC); a swapped request hit an ARP conflict (DHCPDECLINE); or a swapped
                interface got some other address (e.g. a MAC-based DHCP reservation pins the
                service address to S's own interface);
              - always uses the old behaviour, regardless of S: static IP on either interface,
                no Ethernet, NVS unreadable.
            An address obtained while swapped is never adopted as the service address: it
            only changes when S's own interface, asking with its own client-id, is given a
            new one (e.g. the lease expired during a long power cut). Rules: svc_id_* in components/network_mgr/svc_policy.c (host test:
            components/network_mgr/test_host/run.sh).
            Requires CONFIG_LWIP_DHCP_DISABLE_CLIENT_ID=y (the stock option 61 is replaced
            by components/network_mgr/svc_cid.c; a compile-time check enforces it).
            /api/v1/status reports svc_identity, svc_ip, svc_holder and svc_id_mode
            (meanings in network_mgr.h). Bench procedure: docs/test_cases_stability.md test 6e.

    config BITENGINE_WIFI_KEEPALIVE_MS
        int "Wi-Fi uplink keepalive interval (ms, 0 = off)"
        default 5000
        help
            Every N ms, while Wi-Fi is the ACTIVE uplink (i.e. failed over to Wi-Fi),
            send one tiny ICMP echo to the Wi-Fi gateway, pinned to the STA netif.
            Purpose: keep the AP from "parking" an otherwise-idle client. It does NOT
            run while Ethernet is primary and Wi-Fi is idle backup: parking an unused
            interface is harmless and the first failover traffic wakes it anyway.
            2026-09-14 on the production PCB the router (and likely a class of
            consumer APs) stopped delivering DOWNLINK unicast to the gateway for
            3-24s once per ~60s whenever the gateway sent no uplink; any continuous
            uplink made it vanish (docs/产品化TODO T2.21). Uplink from the gateway
            was always clean, only downlink-to-us stalled, so PS/PS_NONE did not
            help. This costs ~64 bytes of airtime per interval.
            Only meaningful when Wi-Fi carries traffic (double-uplink failover to
            Wi-Fi, or clients addressing the Wi-Fi IP). Set 0 to disable. Keep the
            interval well under the AP's ~60s park threshold.

    config BITENGINE_EZSP_HW_FLOWCTRL
        bool "Enable EZSP UART hardware flow control (RTS/CTS)"
        default n
        help
            Drive RTS on IO2 and sample CTS on IO3 for the MG24 link.

            Only turn this on together with an MG24 flashed from the
            460800 + flow-control build (the images in mg24/release/;
            mg24/README.md documents the pairing). Against firmware built with flow
            control None the MG24 never drives our CTS, the line floats,
            and every TX blocks — Zigbee goes completely dead.

            Leave n until both chips are flashed as a pair.

    config BITENGINE_MG24_BOOTLOADER_BAUD
        int "MG24 Gecko Bootloader baud rate"
        default 115200
        help
            Baud rate of the Gecko Bootloader's XMODEM menu on the MG24.

            This is a separate compile-time constant inside the bootloader
            image (SL_SERIAL_UART_BAUD_RATE), not negotiated at runtime, so
            it must match whichever bootloader was flashed by J-Link:

              115200  stock bootloader (SDK default)
              460800  zGateway build — same rate as the NCP application,
                      so the OTA path never has to re-baud

            Set to 460800 at the same time as BITENGINE_EZSP_HW_FLOWCTRL if
            the MG24 bootloader is mg24/release/bootloader-uart-xmodem.s37
            (all production boards).

    config BITENGINE_MG24_REQUIRE_SIGNED_GBL
        bool "Only flash MG24 .gbl images signed with the official key"
        default y
        help
            The gateway checks the ECDSA-P256 signature tag of every .gbl
            before the MG24 is touched, with the public key embedded at
            build time from mg24/release/mg24_gbl_signing_key.pub.
            A signature that does not verify is rejected whatever this
            switch says (400 ncp_signature_invalid); the switch only decides
            what happens to an image that carries NO signature tag:

              y  rejected, 400 ncp_image_unsigned — production setting,
                 see docs/产品化TODO_2026-09-09.md T1.2
              n  developer builds: unsigned images are flashed as before

            The cloud OTA path always requires a signature, regardless.
            Verification happens in the C5, not in the MG24 bootloader, so
            the deployed bootloader is unchanged; the tag is stripped again
            before the XMODEM upload because that bootloader has no key
            provisioned and would reject a signed container after erasing
            the old application.

    config BITENGINE_RS706_WDO_FUNCTIONAL
        bool "RS706 WDO can actually assert MR (AM2 and later)"
        depends on BITENGINE_HAS_HW_WATCHDOG
        default n
        help
            AM1 板上 RS706 的 WDO 经 R55(4.7K)/R57(10K) 与 MR 内部上拉分压后
            仍有 1.16-1.42V，远高于 MR 的 VIL=0.33V——喂不喂狗都不会产生复位
            （docs/hardware/PCB_硬件待确认清单.md X7/A6）。

            置 n 时 wd_feed 仍然翻转 WDI（便于示波器验证链路），但后备完全
            由软件恢复引擎承担。
            AM2 修好这条通路后置 y，喂狗即变为条件喂狗：任务心跳不健康就
            停止喂狗，让硬件在 ~1.6s 后拉复位。这是唯一一条"固件彻底卡死
            也能复位"的路径。

    config BITENGINE_ENABLE_BLE_PROXY
        bool "Enable BLE proxy (passive BLE scan -> MQTT)"
        depends on !BITENGINE_PROFILE_DIRECT
        default n
        help
            直连型里不可选（docs/15 设计第三节）：直连型的 BLE 只经 ble_window 用（配对窗口），
            ble_proxy 会自己初始化 NimBLE 并常驻扫描，两者不能在同一构建里。HA 型不受影响。

            components/ble_proxy 已完整实现（NimBLE 被动扫描 + 30s 限频 + MQTT 上报），
            但**默认关**，因为 BLE 扫描会破坏 802.15.4 的 CCA，让 Zigbee/Thread 收发
            出问题。docs/09 §6.2 当初自我质疑的结论「BLE 扫描干扰极小」已被实测推翻。

            这个开关是 2026-08-17 从 main.c 里一行注释掉的 ble_proxy_init() 改过来的：
            注释不是守卫 —— 它挡不住谁顺手删掉再启用，也不会在任何 VERIFY 里露面。

            ⚠️ 开之前必须先解决与 Zigbee/Thread 的射频共存，否则现象是
            "Zigbee 设备零星丢包/掉线"，而且极难归因到 BLE。

            另：关着它**不省内存**。2026-08-17 做过 A/B 全量构建，
            CONFIG_BT_ENABLED=y/n 两版逐段字节完全相同（HP SRAM 238573 vs 238573）
            —— 因为 ble_proxy_init() 不被调用，链接器把整个归档丢掉了。
            所以别为了省内存去动 BT 相关配置，那条路收益是 0。

    config BITENGINE_ENABLE_OT_CLI
        bool "Enable OpenThread CLI on the USB console (RF lab / diag builds only)"
        default n
        help
            把 OpenThread CLI 接到 USB Serial/JTAG 控制台。为射频实验室测量而加：
            CONFIG_OPENTHREAD_DIAG 一直是 y，但 CLI 从未被初始化，所以 `diag`
            命令至今没有输入口。开了之后可以

                diag start / diag channel 15 / diag power 20 / diag repeat 1 127

            让 C5 的 2.4G 802.15.4 射频连续发调制包，用频谱仪量实际口面功率、
            谱密度、带边与谐波 —— 这正是 docs/hardware/射频功率与认证.md 第三节
            「回读不是证据，以实测为准」要的那种证据。⚠️ 没有连续载波：ESP 端口
            没实现 otPlatDiagRadioTransmitCarrier / TransmitStream，`diag cw` 与
            `diag stream` 返回 NotImplemented（2026-10-09 核实）。步骤见
            docs/test_cases_rf_bench.md 第 3.2 节。

            ⚠️ 出厂必须保持 n，三条理由，每条都足够：

            1. **泄密**：CLI 上 `dataset active -x` 会明文吐出 Thread NetworkKey
               与 PSKc，`factoryreset` 会直接抹掉网络。虽然要物理插 USB 才够得着，
               但这是把一个无认证的管理面永久挂在控制台上。
            2. **吃 4KB 内部 SRAM**：esp_openthread_cli_create_task() 内部是
               xTaskCreate(..., 4096, ...)，落内部内存，我们改不了（IDF 的函数
               不接受栈参数，也没有对应的 deinit）。**推算**（未实测）：dma.min_free
               会从 5319 掉到 1200 出头，而 ot_cli_loop 还要 esp_console_init() +
               linenoise 的行缓冲，实际只会更低 —— 总之**低于硬停判据 6 的 3072
               地板**。所以 diag 构建跑 tools/test_api.sh 时那一条红是预期的，
               不是回退；真要用这个构建做长时间测量，先量一次 /diag/heap 心里有数。
            3. **抢 stdin**：ot_cli_loop 会 esp_console_init() + linenoise 接管
               标准输入，并打印 "> " 提示符与日志交织。

            ⚠️ 还有一条工程约束：IDF **没有**提供 CLI 的 deinit/delete，而
            thread_br_start() 在 stop 之后可能再被调用（失败路径、配网结束后的
            延迟启动）—— 所以调用点必须有一次性守卫，否则重启一次 Thread 就多一个
            ot_cli 任务抢同一个 stdin。

    config BITENGINE_ENABLE_MDNS_LOAD
        bool "Enable synthetic mDNS load generator (scale experiments only)"
        default n
        help
            开放 POST/GET /api/v1/diag/mdns_load，按真实 Matter 设备的线上格式
            连续注册 N 条假服务（instance/host/TXT/subtype 逐项同形状），
            用来在**一块板、零真实设备**的条件下把容量墙推到面前。

            为什么需要：本设备的容量墙是一串**可数的计数/长度上限**，不是内存 ——
            Zigbee 侧固件根本不知道接了几个设备（决策 1 纯字节流透传），Thread 侧
            OT 的表全是编译期预分配。所以验证容量不需要 N 台设备，只需要 N 条记录。
            方案全文见 docs/扩到50设备_2026-08-17.md 的「不买 50 个设备怎么验证」C 节。

            ⚠️ **出厂必须保持 n**：这些记录会**真的播到局域网上**，
            HA / matter-server 会真的看到一堆假 Matter 设备（它们不可达，
            控制器会一直重试）。实验做完 `{"n":0}` 撤回，或直接重启。

            ⚠️ 它**不覆盖 SRP server 与 OT 侧开销**（直接打 mDNS，绕过 SRP）。
            所以必须与 D 方案交叉验证：用网关自己的 SRP client（或一块外部
            Thread 节点）跑通真实链路，比对线上字节数确认两者等价，再用本模块外推。

    config BITENGINE_FAULT_INJECTION
        bool "Enable watchdog fault injection endpoints"
        default n
        help
            开放 POST /api/v1/diag/fault，可注入任务挂起、内存抽干、MG24 静默、
            Thread 射频冻结等故障，用于验证看门狗各层真的会触发
            （docs/04_watchdog_design_v2.md 第十一节，TC-W01~W10）。

            v1 的堆告警/堆重启/泄漏检测三条路径都不可能触发却没人发现，
            根因就是没有这类用例。出厂固件保持 n。

    config BITENGINE_OT_LOG_LEVEL
        int "OpenThread runtime log level (1=CRIT 2=WARN 3=NOTE 4=INFO 5=DEBG)"
        depends on OPENTHREAD_LOG_LEVEL_DYNAMIC
        range 1 5
        default 2
        help
            thread_br 在 esp_openthread_init() 之后用 otLoggingSetLevel() 设的级别，同时决定 ESP 日志里
            "OPENTHREAD" 标签的级别（≥3 才放 INFO）—— IDF 的代播库直接用这个标签打 INFO，不受 OT 级别管。
            默认 2（WARN）：告警与错误照常进 /api/v1/logs（log_store 只留 OPENTHREAD 的 W/E，INFO
            本来就进不去）；压掉的是 USB 串口监视里 OPENTHREAD 的 NOTE 与 INFO（角色变化、Border Agent
            起来这类）—— 要判这些事用 REST（:8081/node/state 等，见 docs/test_cases_factory_provisioning.md TC-07）。
            ⚠️ 出厂固件别调到 3 以上：每条 SRP 注册多打 22 行 INFO，以 115200 波特忙等写进本板没引出的 UART0，
            网关重启后设备成批重注册时会把 IDLE 饿死、任务看门狗 panic（数据见
            docs/test_cases_scale_baseline.md「SRP 代播满载压测」第 2 件）。

    config BITENGINE_DIAG_THREAD_BACKBONE
        bool "Enable Thread backbone switch test endpoint"
        depends on OPENTHREAD_ENABLED
        default n
        help
            开放 POST /api/v1/diag/thread/backbone {"to":"eth"|"wifi"}：运行中把边界路由
            的 backbone 换到指定网口（thread_br_switch_backbone，只拆/建边界路由这一层）。
            用于验证"以太网断线时边界路由跟着换到 WiFi"这条修法，
            见 docs/test_cases_stability.md 测试 6c。
            出厂固件保持 n：产品里换口应由 thread_br 在上行切换时自己做，不该由外部触发。

    config BITENGINE_DIAG_SVC_ID
        bool "Enable service identity override test endpoint (T9.37)"
        depends on BITENGINE_SVC_IDENTITY
        default n
        help
            开放 POST /api/v1/diag/svc_id {"s":"eth"|"wifi"}：把服务身份记录改成指定那张卡、服务地址置为"还不知道"，
            重启后生效（持有者第一次拿到的地址就是新的服务地址）。用于在一块"先插网线装"的板子上模拟
            "先用 WiFi 装、后插网线"，验证双向浮动，见 docs/test_cases_stability.md 测试 6e。
            同时开放 GET /api/v1/diag/svc_id：两张卡的 DHCP 状态（租期、距上次 ACK、T1/T2、身份表与实际发出的身份、
            续租 / 重绑请求数）—— 续租成功时地址不变、IDF 不发事件，只能这样看（测试 6e R5）。
            出厂固件保持 n：服务身份只该在首次安装时由网关自己定。

    config BITENGINE_DIAG_ZB_SNIFF
        bool "Enable Zigbee channel sniffer on the C5 802.15.4 radio"
        depends on OPENTHREAD_ENABLED
        default n
        help
            开放 POST/GET /api/v1/diag/zb_sniff：暂停 Thread，把 C5 的 802.15.4 射频临时调到指定信道、
            开混杂模式，把空中帧原样录下来（最多 60 s / 400 帧），主机侧 tools/zb_sniff.py 解码并用
            ZHA 备份里的网络密钥解密。用于看清 Zigbee 设备与 MG24 之间在空口上到底交换了什么
            （2026-10-07 Sengled 掉线排查）。做法与 H1 核对见 components/thread_br/zb_sniff.c 头注。
            出厂固件保持 n：录制期间 Thread 中断；而且它能录下局域网里任何 802.15.4 设备的帧。

    config BITENGINE_DIAG_THREAD_PENDING
        bool "Enable 802.15.4 pending-table stress test endpoint"
        depends on OPENTHREAD_ENABLED && IEEE802154_ENABLED
        default n
        help
            开放 GET/POST /api/v1/diag/thread/pending：往 802.15.4 帧挂起表里塞入或撤回
            假短地址（router ID 63 段，Thread 永不分配），并回扫描耗时、MAC"收到重复帧"计数、
            子设备状态（含是否 CSL 同步）。用于验证挂起表扩到 ≥ 子设备上限之后，满表时 ACK
            仍然赶得上。步骤与判据见 docs/test_cases_scale_baseline.md「802.15.4 帧挂起表满表压测」。
            出厂固件保持 n：假条目会占掉真子设备的表位。

    config BITENGINE_DIAG_SRP_INJECT
        bool "Enable SRP UPDATE inject test endpoint (scale test D)"
        depends on OPENTHREAD_ENABLED && OPENTHREAD_BORDER_ROUTER
        default n
        help
            开放 POST /api/v1/diag/srp/inject（二进制进、二进制出）：把一条 SRP UPDATE 原样经
            OpenThread 内部 UDP 栈发给本机 SRP server，回它的应答。tools/srp_load.py --inject 用它
            扮演 N 台 SRP 客户端，走完整真实链路（SRP server → advertising proxy → mDNS → 局域网）。
            为什么要绕这一圈：从局域网发往网关自身 OMR 地址的 SRP 包进不了 OT 的 UDP 栈
            （srp_load.py 头注里的证据链），而一块 Thread 开发板只能是一个 SRP host，补不了规模。
            步骤与判据见 docs/test_cases_scale_baseline.md「SRP 代播满载压测」。
            出厂固件保持 n：任何能访问 Web 的人都能借它往 SRP 里塞假设备。

    config BITENGINE_DIAG_COREDUMP
        bool "Enable coredump download endpoint"
        depends on ESP_COREDUMP_ENABLE_TO_FLASH
        default n
        help
            开放 GET /api/v1/diag/coredump：把 coredump 分区里那份镜像原样下载下来，离线解码出
            崩溃那一刻全部任务的回溯：
              esp-coredump info_corefile -t raw -c <下载的文件> <崩溃那一版固件的 .elf>
            ⚠️ ELF 必须是崩溃那一版（镜像里只有地址），刷新固件前先把 build 目录的 .elf 留一份。
            为什么不用 idf.py coredump-info / esptool：读完要芯片级复位，本板以太网在线时会
            卡进下载模式、只能断电恢复（docs/hardware/硬件缺陷档案.md X6）。
            ⚠️ /status 报的复位原因帮不上忙：main.c 在非干净复位后会补一次 esp_restart()，
            panic / 看门狗复位之后看到的一律是 SOFTWARE。
            出厂固件保持 n：镜像里是崩溃那一刻各任务的栈，可能夹着口令、密钥等明文。

    config BITENGINE_DIAG_CRYPTO_RACE
        bool "Run the ECDSA-reset vs RSA/SHA race stress test at boot (T9.47)"
        default n
        help
            诊断固件专用。开机 90 s 后跑一轮对照压测：硬件 ECDSA 验签与硬件大数运算 / SHA 并发，
            ECDSA 锁分别按 v6.0.2 原样（旁路）与修复后各跑两段，每段一行 W 级日志（GET /api/v1/logs）。
            实现与判读见 components/idf_fixes/crypto_race_diag.c。
            出厂固件保持 n：旁路那两段是真把缺陷放出来，网关自己的 TLS / Thread 加密也可能被打坏。

    config BITENGINE_DIAG_HEAP_TRACE
        bool "Enable DMA heap trace diagnostics (failover memory dip)"
        depends on SPIRAM
        select HEAP_USE_HOOKS
        default n
        help
            诊断固件专用。以太网断线时自动开一个 12 s 窗口，逐笔记录 DMA 可用内存上的
            分配（大小、caps、发起任务、何时释放），找出 dma.min_free 低谷那一刻是谁的块
            还占着；GET /api/v1/diag/heaptrace 读结果，POST {"window_s":N} 手动开窗，
            {"window_s":0} 重置。记录表全在 PSRAM，不给每块分配加头部。
            实现与判读见 components/watchdog/wd_heaptrace.c。
            出厂固件保持 n：它给全系统每一次 malloc/free 挂了钩子。

    config BITENGINE_DIAG_HEAP_TRACE_BOOT_MS
        int "Also open a heap-trace window at boot (ms, 0 = off)"
        depends on BITENGINE_DIAG_HEAP_TRACE
        range 0 60000
        default 0
        help
            非 0 时，追踪器初始化（main.c 里，网络起来之前）就开一个这么长的窗口，抓开机过程里的 DMA 低谷 ——
            比如 T9.38：开着 MQTT 开机时 dma.min_free 掉到约 2.1 KB。开机窗口里的分配大多是常驻的，
            "最低点时还占着"的列表会很长：判读要拿开 / 关某个功能的两次开机对比差出来的块。
            窗口占着时以太网断线不再自动开窗（追踪器同一时间只有一个窗口）。

    config BITENGINE_SRP_READVERTISE
        bool "Track SRP-proxied mDNS services"
        depends on OPENTHREAD_ENABLED
        default y
        help
            跟踪 SRP advertising proxy 代播出去的 mDNS 服务（Thread 子设备的
            _matter._tcp 等），并在"SRP 里注册了、mDNS 里却查不到"时告警——
            那通常意味着 proxy 静默发布失败（多半是 mdns 服务表满）。
            这部分只观察、不改动任何记录，开销可忽略，建议保持开启。

            是否**主动撤销并重新宣告**记录由下面的 FORCE_BYE 单独控制。

    config BITENGINE_SRP_READV_FORCE_BYE
        bool "Force goodbye + re-announce (python matter-server only)"
        depends on BITENGINE_SRP_READVERTISE
        default n
        help
            开启后做两件事：开机后把每个代播服务先发 TTL=0 的 goodbye 再重新
            宣告；以及在 esp_restart() 之前再发一次 goodbye。

            ⚠️ 默认关，因为收益只对 **python matter-server** 成立。

            收益（有实证）：python zeroconf 收到 TTL=0 的 PTR 会立即移除缓存并
            回调 Removed，之后同名 PTR 就是 Added —— 而 python matter-server
            只有在 Added 分支才会重建订阅，否则要干等 600s 的电池设备存活超时。

            代价（对任何对端都存在）：
              - 开机后那次：goodbye 与重新宣告之间设备有 BYE_GAP_MS 不可发现
              - 重启前那次：**主动清掉对端缓存**，而缓存正是扛过"网关重启到设备
                重新向 SRP 注册"那段空窗的东西（实测 21-35s，远短于 120s 的
                记录 TTL，本来完全无感）

            2026-08-15 在 matter.js（ghcr.io/matter-js/matterjs-server）上实测：
            发了 goodbye 之后控制器**零反应**，没有任何 offline / Resolving /
            Removed / Pairing request，订阅自始至终没断。也就是说对它只有代价、
            没有收益，而且清缓存这一下恰好落在最脆弱的时刻。

            只有确认对端是 python matter-server 时才开。

            ⚠️ 打开前先跑 docs/test_cases_srp_readvertise.md 的 TC-S03（多设备路径）——
            它至今没在真板上验过；关着时这段代码根本不编译，出厂固件上跑不出任何信息。

    config BITENGINE_SRP_READV_BYE_GAP_MS
        int "Gap between goodbye and re-announce (ms)"
        depends on BITENGINE_SRP_READV_FORCE_BYE
        default 2000
        range 1000 10000
        help
            goodbye 与重新宣告之间的间隔。必须让两者成为对端能分辨的两个
            独立事件：zeroconf 收到 TTL=0 会立即移除缓存并回调 Removed，
            matter-server 自己还有 0.5s 的事件去抖。设为 0 等于什么都没做。

            这段时间内该设备在局域网上不可发现。默认 2000ms。

    config BITENGINE_THREAD_TX_POWER_OVERRIDE
        bool "Force a fixed Thread (802.15.4) TX power, overriding the region setting"
        default n
        help
            ⚠️ **2026-09-15 起这个开关的含义变了**（docs/14）：Thread 功率现在**默认就按
            网关的「射频地区」设置**取值（设置页 →「射频地区」，或 `POST /api/v1/radio/region`）：
            CE 10 / FCC 20 / 其他 8 / 未设置 10 dBm，改地区时立刻生效、不用重启。
            所以出厂关 **不再等于满功率**，而是等于"按地区"。

            开这个开关 = **无视地区**，强制用下面那个固定值。只给射频实验室用
            （`docs/test_cases_rf_bench.md`），出货构建别开 —— 开了之后用户在
            界面上选的地区对 Thread 不起作用，而界面不会说明这件事。

            （以下两段是 09-15 之前的背景，留着说明为什么要管。）

            ⚠️ **C5 自己的 802.15.4（Thread）在没人设功率时就在该芯片功率表的最高一档发射**，
            而且没有任何一处代码选过这个值：IDF 的 PIB 初始化把 16 个信道全填成
            功率表末项（`esp_ieee802154_pib.c:70`），OpenThread 自己**从不调**
            `otPlatRadioSetTransmitPower`（全 OT 源码里只有 factory diags 调它）。
            也就是说这颗射频的功率此前既没人设、也没人看过。

            这和 Zigbee 那颗不是一回事，别混：MG24 的功率由 Z2M/ZHA 每次启动经
            EZSP 写进 NCP，09-15 起由 NCP 按地区封顶（docs/14），网关能读到上限
            （/api/v1/radio/region 的 zigbee.cap_dbm）。**这个开关只管 C5 上的 Thread**。

            开这个开关才会去覆盖。无论开关与否，Thread 启动时都会打一行
            `802.15.4 TX power:` 日志 —— 关着时那行打印的就是本平台功率表的
            上限，这是它唯一的可观测出口。

            认证背景见 docs/hardware/射频功率与认证.md。

    config BITENGINE_THREAD_TX_POWER_DBM
        int "Thread 802.15.4 TX power (dBm)"
        depends on BITENGINE_THREAD_TX_POWER_OVERRIDE
        default 20
        range -24 20
        help
            覆盖值，对 16 个信道一起生效（`esp_ieee802154_set_txpower()` 内部就是
            把功率表 16 项填成同一个数），所以后续换信道不会把它丢掉。

            ⚠️ 驱动会把这个数**向下**吸附到功率表里最近的一档
            （`ieee802154_txpower_convert()`），不是线性可调。低于表首项按表首项、
            高于表末项按表末项，两端都不会报错 —— 所以这里填了不等于就发得出来，
            以实验室实测为准。

            ⚠️ 回读拿不到吸附后的值：`esp_ieee802154_get_txpower()` 返回的是存进
            PIB 的请求值，原样回显。别拿它当"实际功率"的证据。

    config BITENGINE_OTA_CLOUD_URL
        string "Cloud OTA manifest URL (https only)"
        default "https://updates.bitengine.tech/hub/manifest.json"
        help
            设备"检查更新"时去拉的 JSON manifest 地址。必须是 https:// ——
            代码里有硬校验，http 直接拒绝发出请求。

            ⚠️ **这个域名会硬编码进出货固件，出货后换不掉**（换了就得让用户
            手动升级一次，而那正是云 OTA 要避免的场景）。所以：

              * 用你们自己控制的域名做 CNAME，**别**直接写 github.io 或某个
                对象存储的原始地址 —— 将来换托管商 = 失去全部存量设备
              * 默认值 updates.bitengine.tech 是 2026-09-09 定下的出货域名
                （docs/产品化TODO_2026-09-09.md T1.1），DNS 与托管必须一直
                在我们自己手里。固件文件放同目录 hub/bitengine-<ver>.bin，
                manifest 用 tools/make_manifest.py 生成，别手写

            manifest 格式（多余字段会被忽略）：
                {"version":"v0.6.0-3-gabcdef0",
                 "url":"https://.../bitengine-v0.6.0-3-gabcdef0.bin",
                 "size":2166784,
                 "notes":"一行更新说明"}

            ⚠️ url 指向的必须是**签名版** build/bitengine.bin，不是
            bitengine-unsigned.bin。传错了设备会拒装（失败方向是安全的，
            不会变砖），见 docs/guide/固件签名与密钥保管.md。

    config BITENGINE_OTA_CLOUD_TIMEOUT_MS
        int "Cloud OTA HTTP timeout (ms)"
        default 6000
        range 1000 30000
        help
            拉 manifest 和下载固件的超时。

            ⚠️ 拉 manifest 是**同步**的，跑在 httpd 任务里，期间整个 Web 界面
            卡住（webui 是单任务，见 components/webui）。所以这个值就是用户点
            "检查更新"后界面最长的卡顿时间。别往大调 —— 网络不通时用户会以为
            设备死了。6s 是"慢网络能成功"与"卡住不至于吓人"之间的折中。

endmenu
